      "value": "Anti aliasing should not be used anyway, as the game already has anti-aliasing of its own.\n\nWhat do you propose as a solution for the screenspace reflections? Moving to the Deferred rendering path would be an extremely bad idea. Deferred is not suitable for VR for many reasons. Having it be selectable by the world creator could be nice, provided that MSAA can be turned off on runtime (which probably isn't very easy).\n\nThe other bugs you talked about (Bloom and DoF) are caused by keyword overuse. Unity only has room for 256 keywords in a single session, after which any more can no longer be added. As far as I know, this is not fixable on VRChat's end.",
